{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-106072" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transform the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/2}\\,\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2}-y=0\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-106072" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{1/2}\\,\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2}-y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{1/2}\\,\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2} & =y \\\\ \\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}y & ={y}^{1/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{2},\\,q(x)=1,\\,n=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{1/2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}{y}^{1/2}=1.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}z=1\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,z=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-106072" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3cf0c6da9042b24e74d589b9491e2e3980039f1bdc3fb6453a3f9abf7b380cad"} {"question" "q-106072" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-106072" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-106072" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{4}y=\\sqrt{y}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{4},\\,q(x)=1,\\,n=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{1/2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{4}{y}^{1/2}=1.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{4}z=1\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}z=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3cf0c6da9042b24e74d589b9491e2e3980039f1bdc3fb6453a3f9abf7b380cad"} {"question" "q-109018" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109018" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x"] ["math" "2{x}^{4}"] ["math" "4{x}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109018" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{y}}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{2},\\,q(x)={x}^{3},\\,n=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the differential equation by ${y}^{1/2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2}={x}^{3}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{3/2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{1/2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}\\,z={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}\\,z=\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3cf0c6da9042b24e74d589b9491e2e3980039f1bdc3fb6453a3f9abf7b380cad"} {"question" "q-109022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{x}^{2}"] ["math" "3{x}^{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y=\\sqrt{y}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-1,\\,q(x)=1,\\,n=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{1/2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{dy}{dx}-{y}^{1/2}=1.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-z=1\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{2}z=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-1/2)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={e}^{-x/2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x/2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{2}z) & ={e}^{-x/2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ {e}^{-x/2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{2}z{e}^{-x/2} & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x/2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-x/2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-x/2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{e}^{-x/2} & =-{e}^{-x/2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =C{e}^{x/2}-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C={C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{1/2}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{1/2}=C{e}^{x/2}-1\\,⇒\\,y={(C{e}^{x/2}-1)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3cf0c6da9042b24e74d589b9491e2e3980039f1bdc3fb6453a3f9abf7b380cad"} {"question" "q-109029" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109029" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{C{e}^{2x}+x+1}{2}}"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{{e}^{2x}+C}{2}}"] ["math" "y={(C{e}^{x/2}-1)}^{2}"] ["math" "y={(\\frac{x}{C{e}^{x/2}-1})}^{2}"] ["math" "y={({e}^{x/2}-2x+C)}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109029" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={(C{e}^{x/2}-1)}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109170" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\nx\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y={x}^{2}{y}^{3/4}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109170" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y={x}^{2}{y}^{3/4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{y}{x} & =x{y}^{3/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{-1},\\,q(x)=x,\\,n=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{3/4},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{-1}{y}^{1/4}=x.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/4}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{-3/4}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{-1}z=x\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-1}z=\\frac{x}{4}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is now in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{4x},\\,Q(x)=\\frac{x}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/4x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{(1/4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={x}^{1/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={x}^{1/4}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{1/4}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-1}z) & ={x}^{1/4}\\cdot (\\frac{x}{4}) \\\\ {x}^{1/4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-3/4}z & =\\frac{{x}^{5/4}}{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{x}^{1/4}) & =\\frac{{x}^{5/4}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{x}^{1/4})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{x}^{5/4}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{x}^{1/4} & =\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{9/4}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{{x}^{9/4}+C}{9{x}^{1/4}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=9{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{1/4}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/4}=\\frac{{x}^{9/4}+C}{9{x}^{1/4}}\\,⇒\\,y={(\\frac{{x}^{9/4}+C}{9{x}^{1/4}})}^{4}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109170" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3cf0c6da9042b24e74d589b9491e2e3980039f1bdc3fb6453a3f9abf7b380cad"} {"question" "q-109170" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109170" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{4{x}^{5/4}+C}{3{x}^{1/4}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{1/4}+C}{4{x}^{9/4}}"] ["math" "y={(\\frac{C{x}^{1/2}-2}{4{x}^{1/2}})}^{2}"] ["math" "y={(\\frac{{x}^{5/4}+C}{5{x}^{1/4}})}^{4}"] ["math" "y={(\\frac{{x}^{9/4}+C}{9{x}^{1/4}})}^{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"} {"question" "q-109170" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={(\\frac{{x}^{9/4}+C}{9{x}^{1/4}})}^{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065712/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a587b6c7a51674e8098dca4c989f7e73658b6183d02802daa12d0209567b928"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2156 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
